{"path":"string/multibyte/btowc","title":"btowc","titleHtml":"btowc","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/string/multibyte/btowc","section":"string","kind":"page","summary":"Widens a single-byte character c (reinterpreted as unsigned char) to its wide character equivalent.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/string/wide\"><code>&lt;wchar.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">wint_t btowc<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> c <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c95\">(since C95)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Widens a single-byte character <code>c</code> (reinterpreted as <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span></code>) to its wide character equivalent. \n</p><p>Most multibyte character encodings use single-byte codes to represent the characters from the ASCII character set. This function may be used to convert such characters to <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">wchar_t</span></span></code>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  c\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  single-byte character to widen\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">WEOF</span></code> if <code>c</code> is <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/io\">EOF</a></span>\n</p><p>wide character representation of <code>c</code> if <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>c</span></code> is a valid single-byte character in the initial shift state, <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">WEOF</span></code> otherwise.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;wchar.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;locale.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;assert.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">unsigned</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> c<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    wint_t w <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> btowc<span class=\"br0\">(</span>c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>w <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> WEOF<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"The single-byte character&nbsp;%#x widens to&nbsp;%#x<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, c, w<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">else</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"The single-byte character&nbsp;%#x failed to widen<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, c<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>loc <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/c/locale/setlocale\"><span class=\"kw900\">setlocale</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/locale/LC_categories\"><span class=\"kw903\">LC_ALL</span></a>, <span class=\"st0\">\"lt_LT.iso88594\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/error/assert\"><span class=\"kw407\">assert</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>loc<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"In Lithuanian ISO-8859-4 locale:<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'A'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es2\">\\xdf</span>'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// German letter ß (U+00df) in ISO-8859-4</span>\n    try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es2\">\\xf9</span>'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// Lithuanian letter ų (U+0173) in ISO-8859-4</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/c/locale/setlocale\"><span class=\"kw900\">setlocale</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/locale/LC_categories\"><span class=\"kw903\">LC_ALL</span></a>, <span class=\"st0\">\"lt_LT.utf8\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"In Lithuanian UTF-8 locale:<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'A'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es2\">\\xdf</span>'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    try_widen<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es2\">\\xf9</span>'</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>In Lithuanian ISO-8859-4 locale:\nThe single-byte character 0x41 widens to 0x41\nThe single-byte character 0xdf widens to 0xdf\nThe single-byte character 0xf9 widens to 0x173\nIn Lithuanian UTF-8 locale:\nThe single-byte character 0x41 widens to 0x41\nThe single-byte character 0xdf failed to widen\nThe single-byte character 0xf9 failed to widen</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.29.6.1.1 The btowc function (p: 441)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.24.6.1.1 The btowc function (p: 387)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/string/multibyte/wctob\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>wctob</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-c95\">(C95)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   narrows a wide character to a single-byte narrow character, if possible <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/multibyte/btowc\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>btowc</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table></div>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"string","title":"Strings library"},{"path":"string/multibyte","title":"Null-terminated multibyte strings"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"btowc","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Widens a single-byte character c (reinterpreted as unsigned char) to its wide character equivalent."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"c"},{"label":"Return value","note":"WEOF if c is EOF"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"wctob","note":"narrows a wide character to a single-byte narrow character, if possible"}]}]},"standards":["C95"],"wordCount":258,"codeBlockCount":2}
